  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Amaze pivoted sharply in 2025 from a consumer-packaged goods pedigree into a pure-play, creator-powered commerce platform, targeting the growing creator economy. The asset-light model—leveraging third-party manufacturing and fulfillment—enabled top-line expansion as the company onboarded creators and brands seeking to sell globally. However, the transition has yet to deliver operating leverage; commentary points to material profitability pressures and negative cash flows even as platform activity ramps. The narrative is thus mixed: robust structural demand for creator-driven sales exists, but the company currently absorbs higher costs to scale, leaving earnings quality unproven.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership characterized 2025 as a foundational year spent consolidating the Amaze Software acquisition and integrating the platform for “commerce-led growth” in 2026. Year-end shareholder communications struck an optimistic tone, touting milestones and strategic positioning. While the team earnestly executed the repositioning, the lack of near-term profitability and cash generation tempers credibility; the strategic vision is clear, but execution track record on cost discipline remains thin. Management’s ability to convert platform momentum into sustainable unit economics is the central open question for market sentiment.",
